  <page_number>152</page_number>
  <running_head>P. RAMI</running_head>
  <main_text>
    <l n="1" para="true">ῥαξνομέω παρλωόμεον, contra leges a-</l>
    <l n="2">go, bam. At ἐμπολάω emo, lucror, ἡμπόλαον &amp; ςνεπόλαον.</l>
    <l n="3" para="true">Aut si præpositio nihil augeat signifi-</l>
    <l n="4">catum, augmentum fit initio: ut</l>
    <l n="5">ςνέπω ἐωέπον, dico, bam.</l>
    <l n="6">καθεύδω ἐκαθέυδον, dormio, bam. καθίζω</l>
    <l n="7">ἐκαθίζον, sedere facio, bam.</l>
    <l n="8" para="true">Attamen quædam plus significan-</l>
    <l n="9">tia augentur initio: ut</l>
    <l n="10">ἀμφιβάλλω ἠμφίβαλλον, dubito, bam.</l>
    <l n="11" para="true">
      <i>Augmentum duplex.</i> Duo faciunt</l>
    <l n="12">utrunque simul:</l>
    <l n="13">ςνοχλέω ἐωοχλέον, turbo, bam.</l>
    <l n="14">ἀνορθόω ἐωορθοον, corrigo, bam.</l>
    <l n="15" para="true">
      <i>Attice incrementum syllabicum tem-</i>
    </l>
    <l n="16">
      <i>poraliter augetur</i>:</l>
    <l n="17">ut μέλλω debeo, ἐμελλον debebam, Attice</l>
    <l n="18">ἠμελλον. etiam in medio composi-</l>
    <l n="19">ti: ut ἀπολαύω fruor, ἀπέλαυον, Atti-</l>
    <l n="20">ce ἀπήλαυον, fruebar. Sic poetæ</l>
    <l n="21">metri</l>
  </main_text>
  <notes />
